# The build of groups on a device with groups that hold no particle, under
# compute-sanitizer (#413). A chunk of fewer than four particles makes
# four groups, some of them empty; the lists read the fourth lane of the
# wrapped position at the first place of every group, which the boxes wrote
# only for a place with a particle. initcheck found the read on JAC of the
# Amber suite; here a fluid of 129 atoms in one column, cut into chunks of
# 64, 64, and 1, has three empty groups at its first build
# (Inputs/short_chunk.py). No access beyond a buffer, no read of memory
# that nothing has written, and no race in shared memory.
#
# REQUIRES: cuda, compute-sanitizer
#
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t
# RUN: %python %S/Inputs/short_chunk.py %t
# RUN: cd %t && %compute_sanitizer --tool memcheck --error-exitcode 1 mdir run run.toml 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s
# RUN: cd %t && %compute_sanitizer --tool initcheck --error-exitcode 1 mdir run run.toml 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s
# RUN: cd %t && %compute_sanitizer --tool racecheck --error-exitcode 1 mdir run run.toml 2>&1 \
# RUN:   | FileCheck %s --check-prefix=RACE

# CHECK: ERROR SUMMARY: 0 errors
# RACE: RACECHECK SUMMARY: 0 hazards displayed (0 errors, 0 warnings)
